{title: Here I Am to Worship (FJ_158_en)}
{song_number: 158}
{language: en}

{comment: Verse 1}
[E]Light of the world, You [B]stepped down into [F#m]darkness,
[E]opened my eyes, [B]let me [A]see.
[E]Beauty that [B]made this heart [F#m]adore You,
[E]hope of a [B]life spent with [A]You.

{comment: Chorus}
So here I [A]am to [B]worship, here I [E]am to bow down,
here I [B]am to say that [E]You're my God.
And You're alto[A]gether [E]lovely, altogether worthy,
alto[B]gether [E]wonderful to [A]me.

{comment: Verse 2}
[E]King of all days, oh [B]so highly ex[F#m]alted,
[E]glorious in heaven [B]a[A]bove.
[E]Humbly You [B]came to the [F#m]earth You created,
[E]all for love's [B]sake became [A]poor.

{comment: Additional section}
And I'll [A]never [B]know how [E]much it cost
to see [B]my sin up[E]on that cross.
{comment: Repeat additional section; finish with chorus}
